{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"argv": ["git", "commit", "-m", "E030: close H1 as not_evaluated -- B1's statistic measured length and coincidence (F050, A9 null, length-matched sign flip); A8 held-out separation fires\n\nThe pair-level recurrence gate fired (diff 0.1338 [0.0997, 0.1687]) but its\nown printed linkage is ordinary English tokens between unrelated comments,\nits permutation null explains the arm difference (0.3493 vs 0.2925 +/- 0.012),\nand the length-matched recomputation reverses the sign (-0.0735). C1's pilot\nnever ran; A2's 1-of-6 and A6's unreachable 0.60 gate stand as recorded.\nA8 on the held-out 30/30 read: treatment 16/25 = 0.64 vs control 1/28 = 0.036,\nso the departure-framing population is real and distinct even though the\nclause-recurrence ruler is falsified. Protocol amendments 4-9 and the\nexperiment README record the gates, the withdrawn verdicts, and one reader's\npass as one reader's pass."], "cwd": "/home/ubuntu/think-free", "duration_ms": 300, "exit_code": 0, "log": "sessions/2026-10-05-020-e030-test-whether-departure-accounts-peo/commands.log", "log_line_end": 348, "log_line_start": 341, "redactions": [], "summary": "$ git commit -m E030: close H1 as not_evaluated -- B1's statistic measured length and coincidence (F050, A9 null, length-matched sign flip); A"}, "duration_ms": 300, "exit_code": 0, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "command", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 26, "session": "2026-10-05-020-e030-test-whether-departure-accounts-peo", "ts": "2026-10-05T22:39:35+00:00"}
